From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: power key on PL4

Measured at the device on 2026-09-08 (Paket G3, doku/nachtlog/S38): the front
button sits on PL4, active low, idle 1 / pressed 0, with an external pull-up.
Stock says the same in `standby_param` (`power_key = "PL4"`,
`key_debounce = <50>`), but that node is only read by U-Boot and the ARISC --
Linux never saw the key so far.

`gpio-keys` is enough here: PL4 offers gpio_in (mux 0) and PL_EINT4 (mux 6) in
pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c, so gpiod_to_irq() gives the driver a real interrupt
instead of a poll loop, and the R_PIO irqchip has .irq_set_wake, so the
`wakeup-source` flag does not make suspend fail.

No LED node: the front LED follows PB5 (fan/backlight power), there is no
separate LED to drive -- see the measurements in
analyse/boot/arbeit/REGELN.md.

Needs CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO=y, see the companion defconfig patch
0139b-board-defconfig-enable-keyboard-gpio.patch.
---
diff -Nur a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/thermal/thermal.h>
 
 / {
@@ -2333,6 +2334,33 @@
 	};
 
 	/*
+	 * Power button on PL4 -- the pin stock names in `standby_param`
+	 * (`power_key = "PL4"`, `key_debounce = <50>`). Measured on the
+	 * device 2026-09-08: idle reads 1, pressed reads 0, so the board
+	 * carries an external pull-up and no internal bias is set here.
+	 *
+	 * No pinctrl state on purpose: gpiolib muxes the pin to gpio_in when
+	 * the driver claims it, and the irq path re-muxes it to PL_EINT4
+	 * (mux 6, see pinctrl-sun50i-h713-r.c). A pinctrl-0 on this node
+	 * would only claim the same pin a second time.
+	 *
+	 * `wakeup-source` keeps the key armed across suspend; the R_PIO
+	 * irqchip implements .irq_set_wake, so enable_irq_wake() succeeds.
+	 * Actually waking the SoC out of standby stays the ARISC's job.
+	 */
+	gpio_keys: gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		key-power {
+			label = "power";
+			gpios = <&r_pio 0 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PL4 */
+			linux,code = <KEY_POWER>;
+			debounce-interval = <50>;	/* ms, stock value */
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+	};
+
+	/*
 	 * ADC-based keyboard (6 buttons on LRADC channel 0).
 	 * Uses mainline adc-keys driver with LRADC IIO provider.
 	 * Voltage thresholds from stock DTS keyboard@2009800 node.
